---
layout: default
title: API
---

<h2>API</h2>
<p>Uses This has a very tiny (and completely static!) API.</p>

<h3>Endpoints</h3>
<p>Every endpoint listed is available via a GET request. You can also view this list as <a href="/api/openapi.json" title="The OpenAPI spec for the Uses This API.">an OpenAPI spec</a>.</p>

<ul id="api">
<% @site.data[:openapi].paths.each_pair do |path, endpoint| %>
  <li>
    <strong><%= endpoint.get.summary %></strong><br>
    <span class="summary"><a href="<%= path %>" title="An API method that <%= endpoint.get.description.downcase %>">https://usesthis.com<%= path %></a></summary><br>
  <%= endpoint.get.description %>.
  <% if endpoint.get.description.include?("paginated") %>Takes a <code>page</code> parameter.<% end %>
<% end %>
</ul>
